a - primary weapon
b - blindfold
c - secondary weapon
f - sack
k - key
l - lamp
m - magic marker (kept in bag until needed though)
s - stethoscope
t - tinning kit (when I manage to get one)
u - unicorn horn
w - whistle
z - touchstone (when I manage to get one)
B - bag of holding (normally kept in sack until needed)
F - pick-axe

The f and F are historical, I think from when I played archaeologists
a lot and used those; many of the others correspond with the item
letter. I've never really thought about making sure something safe is
at "e" and "y" but it's a good idea.



